# Build output and runtime state. The runnable jar bundles every dependency;
# committing a jar once was enough of a lesson.
target/
logs/

# Sheriff's own state files, dropped at the root of whatever is mounted.
sheriff_errors.json
sheriff_summary.json
sheriff_tracked_files.json

# The extracted rule catalog, in both shapes. Not committed on purpose: it is
# not this project's content, it is read out of Sheriff's proprietary image by
# --extract-rules, down to the source of the fixer scripts it ships. Generate
# your own against the image you have access to:
#
#   java -jar target/sheriff-mcp.jar --agent --extract-rules
#
# Everything here degrades gracefully without it -- the analysis runs against
# Sheriff itself either way; only the rule lookups go quiet.
rules_catalog.json
SHERIFF_RULES.md
